  "title": "Structure of Complexes",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "For transition metal complexes, the coordination number is related to the geometry around the central metal ion. The most common structures of the complexes in coordination compounds are linear, square planar, tetrahedral, and octahedral, corresponding to coordination numbers of 2, 4, 4, and 6, respectively. Coordination numbers greater than 6 are less common and yield a variety of structures. Structures of some typical coordination complexes are shown in the table below."
              }
